{"text": "los\n\nJoby Freeman Youn:\nas\n\nRELEVANT EMPLOYMENT\nOffice of Congressman Austin Scott, GA-08, Washington, D.C. ~ Chief of Staff (January 2011-Present)\n* Supervise staff of 18 in three offices (Washington D.C., Tifton, GA and Warmer Robins, GA)\n* Oversee all communication activities, including messaging and branding strategy, proactive press\noutreach and response, franked mail campaign with an average yearly budget of $150,\ndigita/social media outreach with an average Yeanly budget oP GOON ST OIE (Se, dco\n\u00a9 Oversee all legislative activities, inefuding agriculture and defense portfolios, in support of Rep.\nScott's service on the Armed Services Committee and the Agriculture Committee\n\u2018+ Oversee all constituent services and correspondence in service of 700,000+ constituents\n* Supervise and perform relationship management, outreach, and communication with numerous\nstakeholders concemed with Rep. Scott's committee work and district representation\n* Coordinated 2011 Republican freshman class initiatives on behalf of Rep. Scott in his role as\nClass President, including class messaging initiatives and group press conferences\nAustin Scott for Congress, Macon, GA - Campaign Manager (2010)\n* Developed and executed overall messaging strategy in winning 2010 challenger campaign,\nincluding positive branding of the candidate and response to negative attacks\n* Planned and executed a successful $1 million fundraising effort in 2010\nCoordinated an integrated $1 million communications plan, including TV, radio, direct mail and\n\ndigital campaigns in 21 Georgia counties and three media markets\nManaged press relations through the preparation and booking of the candidate for print, TV and\nradio appearances as well as drafting of statements and press releases\n* Organized and executed five month grassroots mobilization plan, including volunteer recruitment\nand coordination, voter ID, and voter contact through phone and door-to-door campaigns\n\u00a9 Advised on campaign strategy and execution of 2016 re-election effort in Republican primary\nOffice of the Lt. Governor of Georgia, Atlanta, GA ~ Deputy Legislative Counsel (Jan. 2010-July 2010)\n\u00a9 Served as floor staff and legislative liaison to St during legislative session in\nsupport of the Lt. Governor's role as President of the Georgia State Senate\n* Collaborated with Governor's Office, House leadership and members, policy staff, legislative\ncounsel, and outside stakeholders to craft legislation\n* Drafted enacted legislation conceming state construction contracts, eciminal code, ethics laws,\nand the indigent defense system\n* Coordinated 2010 Special Council on Tax Reform and the Lt. Governor's Budget Task Force\nBray & Johnson, Attorneys at Law, Canton, GA - Summer Associate (Summer 2008)\n* Bray & Johnson is a general practice law involved primarily in civil litigation and real estate\n\u2018+ Assisted in trial preparation, drafted documents, and performed legal research for real estate\ntransactions, personal injury, worker's compensation, condemnation, and re-zoning proceedings\nPriti Suri and Associates, New Delhi, India Summer Associate (Summer 2007)\n* PSA is an Indian law firm specializing in corporate and commercial law, cross-border\ntransactions, and joint ventures in India\n\u00a9 Formulated and drafted counterclaims and defense to counterclaims in multimillion-dollar\ncorporate arbitration proceedings between two international litigants\nPrepared briefing materials on Indian contract and arbitration law for arbitration proceedings\nDratted bulletins for clients summarizing developments in Indian economic regulations relevant\nto foreign investment in India\n\nEDUCATION\n\u2018The University of Georgia School of Law \u2018Athens, Georgia\nJuris Doctor, Sohn and Mary Franklin Scholarship Recipient May 2009\n/ The University of Georgia\n\nBachelor of Aris ~ Communication, Bachelor of Arts ~ History December 2005",
